# .shellcheckrc - static analysis config (P10.2).
# SC2230-worthy strictness consistent with the project style: `command -v`
# over `which`, quoted expansions, `local` declarations, `set -euo pipefail`.
#
# Disabled checks are false positives for THIS architecture, not laxity:
#   SC1090  the libs are sourced with a computed path (`. "$root/lib/$name.sh"`);
#           ShellCheck cannot follow a non-constant source. The sourcing is
#           guarded by an existence check at every call site.
#   SC2034  the libs are a sourced library: a variable set in lib/cli.sh is
#           consumed in lib/bootstrap.sh. ShellCheck analyses one file at a
#           time and cannot see cross-file usage through `source`.
#   SC2043  `for cmd in dirname` is an intentional single-iteration loop: it
#           exists to assert a tool is on PATH with a uniform error path.
#   SC2261  `} >&"$fd" 2>/dev/null` duplicates a VARIABLE fd to stdout and
#           sends stderr to /dev/null. When $fd is 2 the two targets differ
#           (stdout->2, stderr->/dev/null); ShellCheck cannot prove $fd != 2.

shell=bash
severity=warning

disable=SC1090,SC2034,SC2043,SC2261
